The type of a module instance is similar to a structure corresponding to the port signature of the module. Note: Instance types are not compatible with structure types because only the ports which are accessed on a particular instance are included in the resulting type. module Adder(a: uint<8>, b: uint<8>) -> (sum: uint<9>) { sum = a + b;
