Modules enable hierarchical design by encapsulating reusable functionality. A module is defined by a name, an optional list of parameters, and a list of input and output ports. module FullAdder( a: bool, b: bool, carry_in: bool,
) -> ( sum: bool, carry_out: bool,
) { let xor1 = a xor b sum = carry_in xor xor1 carry_out = (carry_in and xor1) or (a and b)
} # module Top() -> () {}

